                        "sense_id": "4a08a9a3-e383-3e14-9e8b-c9db34f48603",
                        "entry_id": "86c2c39e-3aa0-3759-951a-05d4702d7faf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "diminutive of ве́тер (véter): wind, breeze"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "diminutive",
                            "form-of"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "47f3ad0d-1482-4b43-acae-dc1d216b6dce",
                                "sense_id": "4a08a9a3-e383-3e14-9e8b-c9db34f48603",
                                "text": "Све́жий, у́тренний ветеро́к чуть-чу́ть поду́л с се́вера. Алекса́ндр слегка́ вздро́гнул, и от ветерка́ и от воспомина́ния, пото́м зевну́л и, заку́тавшись в плащ, погрузи́лся в мечты́.",
                                "translation": "A fresh morning breeze was blowing gently from the south. Alexander was shivering a little, both from the breeze and from his memories. He yawned and, wrapping himself in his cloak, gave himself over to his dreams.",
                                "english": "A fresh morning breeze was blowing gently from the south. Alexander was shivering a little, both from the breeze and from his memories. He yawned and, wrapping himself in his cloak, gave himself over to his dreams."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
